# fixture-expectation-for: Sassy-Dog/velovate
# fixture-expectation-source: the repo's committed .github/dependabot.yml (hand-written, no
#   generated-by marker; also committed verbatim as
#   scripts/fixtures/legacy-markers/velovate-dependabot.fixture).
# fixture-note: the DIRECTORIES below reproduce every directory that file declares — 12 nuget
#   project folders, 4 pubspecs (including one nested under another), 3 Dockerfile folders,
#   /apps/mobile/android, / for actions, and the 4 JS workspace directories. Three deliberate
#   differences remain, and none of them is a location bug:
#     1. ECOSYSTEM NAME. The JS lanes render as `bun`, not `npm`: the repo has a root bun.lock, and
#        setup-deps has classified that as the native bun ecosystem since it GA'd (2025-02). That
#        predates this fixture and is a policy, not a layout, difference.
#     2. ONE EXTRA JS LANE. /media/hyperframes/velovate-team-promo holds a real tracked
#        package.json that the hand-written file omits. It is not vendored (no templates/,
#        fixtures/, examples/ segment), so the derivation counts it. A repo that wants it excluded
#        should say so in the file, not rely on the probe overlooking it.
#     3. LANE GROUPING IS NOT DERIVABLE. The committed file folds those 12 nuget folders into TWO
#        entries via the plural `directories:` key (an api lane and a cli lane) and the 3 docker
#        folders into one, each with its own commit-message prefix, schedule and ignore rules —
#        editorial choices about how PRs should arrive, which no probe can infer. The render emits
#        one entry per (ecosystem, directory) pair instead. Same coverage, more entries; each entry
#        still carries its own groups, so this does not reopen the ungrouped-PR-flood problem.
#   velovate is hand-written and unmarked, so setup-deps reports and skips it either way — this
#   fixture exists to show the generator could now serve that layout, not to propose replacing it.
# ---8<--- ecosystem<TAB>directory, one rendered lane per line
